label("10",(0,0)--(0,10),W);
[/asy] <think> The width of the rectangle is $10,$ and its area is $100 + 10h,$ so its height is $10 + h.$ Therefore, the height of the circle segment above the rectangle is $\frac12 h,$ so the height of the whole top pipe is $10 + \frac12 h,$ as shown in the diagram above. Simplifying, $\frac32 h = 15,$ so $h = \boxed{10}.$ </think> </think>

